      "start": 0.56,
      "end": 2.37,
      "text": "Hi! How are you doing these days?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 9.26,
      "end": 15.97,
      "text": "Ideally a dry day that's mild, not too hot and not freezing. Most paints also need a few hours without rain after you finish."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 19.89,
      "end": 25.6,
      "text": "Usually that's fine. Check the can, many exterior paints are rain resistant after a few hours of drying."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 35.04,
      "end": 40.79,
      "text": "Strong sun can make paint dry too fast and leave marks. Paint that side in the morning while it's still shaded."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 45.76,
      "end": 50.9,
      "text": "Then Wednesday morning it is. Just wait until any dew on the wood has dried off before you start."
    }
